  nonce: b076  # b076
  message: "ADR-0057 (2026-09-18) is now the ruling this row builds on — it was recorded as building on none. When the pyright backend lands, its records for a declaration tree-sitter also emitted go through the same merge pass (WI-kokiz-tilam-bohos-tivat-fogil-bijoj-munad-gazid) and provenance slot (WI-binis-hulud-hivir-nojup-lohob-rotor-javar-gofat) as the Rust arms; the config default (WI-hukuf-juniz-zudoh-tivag-kapad-nobuz-komil-rasis) applies per attribute. ADR-0057 §9 states this is not a Rust feature. Nothing here changes this row's own prerequisites (npm allowlist check, stubs in the analysed repo)."  # b076
- op: discuss  # b97a
  at: '2026-09-19T10:03:06Z'  # b97a
  by: agent  # b97a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b97a
  clock: 6  # b97a
  nonce: b97a  # b97a
  message: "MEASUREMENT FIRST, as this row's own notes asked (2026-09-19, dev e60e6abe43): two-arm diff on hypergumbo-core/src (179 files) — the real analyze_python vs scip-python 0.6.6 (npm, allowlisted; 40 s, 2.1 GB RSS) through the shared hypergumbo_core.scip importer, a temporary `python_scip` registration (anchor as_emitted/token), the ADR-0057 merge pass and `hypergumbo backend-agreement`. Full write-up: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_09192026_1215.md.\n\nTHE ANSWER TO \"what would pyright give us that rust-analyzer measurably did not\": of the syntax arm's 5,048 method-construct call edges left as external stubs (untypeable receivers), 4,831 (95.7%) have a scip-python occurrence at the same site naming the same callee — pyright typed the receiver: 4,654 stdlib (builtins.str 1,080, dict 828, list 733, pathlib.Path 441, set 288, re.Pattern/re.Match 168 each), 99 in-repo, 78 third-party (tree-sitter, numpy, PyYAML, rich). Rust measured 0. In-repo call overlap: 3,162 both arms, 399 SCIP-only, 154 syntax-only; 3,961 corroborated; 98 stubs superseded (§14). kind agreement 4,721/4,723 (the Python arms agree where the Rust arms did not); name 3,024/1,699 (`Type.member` vs `member`); is_exported 2,054/2,669 null←false (INV-huboz at scale).\n\nTWO IMPORTER GAPS HAD TO BE FIXED TO MEASURE ANYTHING (backend-neutral, landing as their own PR): scip-python leaves Document.language empty on every document (everything landed in `unknown`, nothing paired — fixed: extension fallback via the taxonomy) and declares SymbolInformation.kind == 0 on all 17,851 symbols (WI-gapup's declared-kind rule typed every occurrence `references`, zero `calls` — fixed: when the producer is silent the SCIP descriptor grammar decides, a declared kind still wins).\n\nWHAT THE WRAPPER MUST DO THAT THE RUST ONE DOES NOT: carry EXTERNAL references (stdlib/third-party, which resolve_symbol currently drops) as external stub edges with the receiver's module on the same dst id shape the syntax arm mints, so the merge pass folds them and unknown_receiver_scope (INV-fibis/INV-nuhun's metric) sees a module. Carried questions: 4,634 `parameter` SCIP-only Symbols (the syntax arm emits none), 179 module `declaration` records, INV-huboz on is_exported. Proceeding to build (non-executing backend → ADR-0045's deferred config-tier opt-in wiring; §12 recorded fixture from a small sample project, not the 12.8 MB index)."  # b97a
- op: discuss  # e772
  at: '2026-09-19T10:13:30Z'  # e772
  by: agent  # e772
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e772
  clock: 7  # e772
  nonce: e772  # e772
  message: "CORRECTION to the 95.7% above: that ratio is over all 5,048 method-construct stubs, 915 of which the syntax arm had already typed with a module. Over the 4,133 MODULE-LESS stubs — the population unknown_receiver_scope counts — scip-python types 3,973 at the same site and callee (96.1%: 3,840 stdlib, 96 in-repo, 37 third-party). Where both arms typed, the module agrees 743 / differs 115, every difference being SCIP naming the defining class or module (pathlib.PurePath for a Path method; builtins.dict where the syntax arm said typing.Any; sqlite3.dbapi2 for sqlite3) — the backend's answer is the more precise one, not a contradiction. The external-callee id shape the backend must mint to be comparable: `python:{module_path}:0-0:{name}:unresolved` with dst_ref {lang, module_path, name}, the syntax arm's own (ir.py ~820)."  # e772
