- op: discuss  # a9ab
  at: '2026-09-19T11:45:22Z'  # a9ab
  by: agent  # a9ab
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a9ab
  clock: 9  # a9ab
  nonce: a9ab  # a9ab
  message: "Done in PR #1083 (dev ea22d7023c), in two steps as this row's own notes asked: MEASURE first (the two discussion entries above: on hypergumbo-core, scip-python types 3,973 of the 4,133 method-call receivers the syntax arm left module-less, 96.1%, where the Rust arm measured 0; kind agreement 4,721/4,723), fix the two shared-importer gaps that measurement exposed (PR #1082), THEN build the wrapper.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. `packages/hypergumbo-lang-scip-python` (pipx extra `scip-python`; producer `npm install -g @sourcegraph/scip-python@0.6.6`), registered `scip_python`: backend `scip`, languages [\"python\"], executes_analysed_code=False, merge anchor name-as-emitted over the identifier token (ADR-0057 §10) — the ast `python` analyzer's anchor, declared for this partner in WI-kokiz, pairs with it unchanged. Modules gate / invoke / translate / analyzer mirror the rust-analyzer package; the failure taxonomy travels as pass-silence codes (dependency_unavailable / pass_crashed / unreported) and a completed run that indexed nothing is a run, not a skip.\n\nTHE ADR-0045 DEFERRAL FIRED: this is the first non-executing backend, so ruling 4's config tiers are wired — `resolve_optin` takes the merged config decision below the environment; `[backends] scip_python = true|false` is accepted in either tier for exactly the registry's `config_optin_backends()` (alternative arms declaring executes_analysed_code=False), project replacing user, and still refused as a trust key for the executing ones; both lists derive from one declaration. `--backend scip-python` (integration + binary checked, exit 2 naming the install line otherwise), `HYPERGUMBO_SCIP_PYTHON=1`, `--backend tree-sitter` = explicit OFF for every opt-in backend. `resolved_backend_set` names both arms so the results cache keys a Python two-arm run separately (WI-givib).\n\nTHE ONE THING THE RUST ARM NEVER DID: the translation keeps the receiver's module on external callees — `python:pathlib.Path:0-0:glob:unresolved` with `dst_ref` and `call_construct`, the syntax arm's own id shape (ir.format_legacy_dst) — and drops what the syntax arm never models (parameter symbols, per-module `__init__` declarations).\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE. Recorded fixture (ADR-0057 §12): `recorded/sample_project/` (3 files) + the scip-python 0.6.6 `index.scip` (project_root normalised). test_scip_python_recorded_fixtures.py: the recording is what its module says (3 docs, 24 global symbols, empty Document.language, kind 0 everywhere, 29 stdlib occurrences); under the declared anchors 10 of 11 SCIP records pair with all 10 syntax-arm records, 0 ambiguous, kind agrees 10/10; the merge pass folds 10 and corroborates 7; the instrument reproduces the pinned per-attribute and edge tallies (external calls: BOTH 2 where the syntax arm already knew the module — identical ids fold for free — scip-only 6, python-only 11); and of the syntax arm's 7 module-less stubs, 6 gain a typed twin at the same site and the 7th (`label`, a property) is superseded by the SCIP arm's RESOLVED call (§14). CLI: `--backend scip-python` with the wrapper missing → exit 2 naming hypergumbo-lang-scip-python; with the binary missing → exit 2 with the npm line; present → HYPERGUMBO_SCIP_PYTHON=1; `tree-sitter` → both env vars \"0\". Config: a project `.hypergumbo.toml` `[backends] scip_python = true` makes the gate True with no env var; `'yes'` (non-bool) is refused naming the file; an executing backend beside it is still a trust key. 822-file slice green in 12 chunks; 100% on every changed source file (core: backend_selection, scip_python_install, user_config, analyze/registry, cli, linkers/pyffi + inherited_calls + type_hierarchy; the whole new package).\n\nSTRUCTURAL CONSEQUENCES A SECOND PRODUCER FORCED (all caught by existing guards): pyffi's, inherited_calls' and type_hierarchy's depends_on producer sets gained `scip_python` (as rust_analyzer was added in WI-juzig); the recorded-input lint now treats `python` as an incumbent; the architecture generator's package list gained the package. The hand-maintained producer sets are a smell noted in the lab notebook (derivable from the registry), not fixed here.\n\nNOT DONE, STATED: no `install-scip-python` command (a global npm prefix is the user's choice; the error message carries the line); no installed-but-not-enabled nudge for this backend; the fold of a module-less stub into its typed twin at one call site — the last mile that makes the 96.1% visible to unknown_receiver_scope — is WI-hupod, needs_human_review, because §11 makes dst identity; the 179 per-module `declaration` records and 4,634 parameter symbols are dropped rather than modelled; INV-huboz (None beats False on is_exported) now shows on 2,669 records in the Python two-arm.\n\nNOT ASSERTED: the item's \"LIKELY CLOSES\" list (INV-mumov, WI-sitos, WI-jojuv) — each closes on its own repro, not on this landing; the 96.1% is hypergumbo-core, one repository; dependency typing depends on the analysed repo's environment (stubs installed), unmeasured beyond the stdlib."  # a9ab
